# solen — environment knob names (documentation only, never real values).
#
# Copy nothing from this file into a tracked file with real values. Values
# live exclusively in GitHub Actions secrets (CI) or a local, untracked
# .envrc.local. Nothing below is ever echoed: inspect presence only, e.g.
# `${HARBOR_USERNAME:-<unset>}` / `${HARBOR_ROBOT_SECRET:+set}` — the same
# idiom .github/workflows/ci-publish.yml uses around its Harbor probe.

# --- Harbor robot credential (private `solen` project) -------------------
# One robot account backs BOTH Harbor roles in this repo:
#   * the registry build cache (solen/build-cache, pull+push), and
#   * the content-addressed toolcache mirror (solen/toolcache-<tool>-<arch>,
#     SINGLE-LEVEL repo names).
#
# The credential EXISTS and works: the same secret authenticates the
# solen/build-cache pushes and obtained scoped tokens during CI run
# 39018544362 (the 12/12 mirror-push 502s there happened at the
# config-blob POST — after auth — because Harbor parses the first path
# segment as the project and mishandles the nested two-segment form; the
# single-level naming is the fix). The earlier claim here and in commit
# a10b960 that "there is NO robot credential provisioned yet" was FALSE
# and is retracted.
#
# PULL AND PUSH BOTH REQUIRE CREDENTIALS on this project: it is private and
# anonymous access was measured unavailable (GET /v2/ -> 401 Bearer
# challenge; an anonymous token's claims carry "actions": [] and the manifest
# fetch answers "unauthorized to access repository").
#
# Absence semantics remain by design (defensive): if a secret ever stops
# being visible in a job scope, the ci-publish mirror-artefacts push job
# and the per-leg toolcache staging steps skip cleanly and every build
# behaves exactly as it did before the mirror existed (upstream downloads).
# The robot account itself is NOT the missing piece. The robot needs
# pull+push on solen/build-cache and pull+push on each single-level
# solen/toolcache-* repo (pull on those is used by the build legs' staging
# step).
HARBOR_USERNAME=
HARBOR_ROBOT_SECRET=
